# DataGuard Universal Agent Rules

## Authority

1. Follow system/developer instructions and explicit user intent.
2. Read `AGENTS.md` and `rules/workspace_governance.md` before creating, moving, or deleting workspace paths.
3. Use `plans/2026-08-20-workspace-rationalization.md` for cleanup classification and decision gates.

## Working rules

- Production DataGuard source is `src/`; production tests are the DataGuard test projects under `tests/`.
- Documentation and knowledge belong in `docs/`, `plans/`, `research/`, `grants/`, and `brainstorm/`; operational automation belongs in `.github/`, `.githooks/`, `scripts/`, and `tools/`.
- Update documentation when an observable DataGuard contract changes; run the matching build, test, workflow, container, or documentation validator.
- Do not create arbitrary root paths or generated artifacts. Use policy-approved ignored locations for temporary work.

## Cleanup and safety

- Do not delete tracked source, research, legal text, agent configuration, or local session state from an absence search alone.
- Preserve WIP and require an owner-approved `from → keep | extract | rewrite | remove` manifest before irreversible cleanup.
- Do not expose secrets, credentials, tokens, private session state, or handoff content.

